  "question": {
    "text": "The number of structural isomers for <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msub></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Firstly we calculate DU (Degree of unsaturation) of given molecular formula as :-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DU</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DU</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;possibility is for alkanes only.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0333_641c08137e8d.png\" style=\"width: 262px; height: 30px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0333_7a96ed9662ee.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 82px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0333_548e2db02df4.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 74px;\" /></p><p>(PCC stands for parent carbon chain)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Total structural isomers of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0333_d67676ca6574.png\" style=\"width: 365px; height: 180px;\" /></p>"
  }
